# Cadence Lab configuration. install.sh copies this file to .env (mode 600),
# fills in the mode and generates the secrets. .env is never committed.
#
# Both compose and the scripts read this file (the scripts as shell), so keep
# one KEY=value per line and quote values that contain spaces.
#
# After editing .env run
#
#   export CADENCE_VERSION=$(cat VERSION) && docker compose up -d
#
# compose re-reads the environment and recreates only the containers whose
# settings changed.

# --- installation ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The name of this installation on the machine: the Docker Compose project of
# its containers, volumes and network. Not a project inside Cadence Lab - one
# installation holds any number of teams and projects. install.sh writes it
# from --name (default cadence); a second installation on the same machine
# needs a name of its own. Never change it on a live installation: its
# volumes carry the name, and under a new one compose would start empty ones.
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=cadence

# --- mode ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# tls    Caddy serves SDLC_DOMAIN over HTTPS with a Let's Encrypt certificate.
#        Needs a DNS A/AAAA record pointing at this machine and ports 80 and
#        443 reachable from the internet.
# proxy  plain HTTP on CADENCE_HTTP_ADDR behind your own reverse proxy, which
#        terminates TLS. No domain or ACME needed here.
CADENCE_MODE=tls
# Must match CADENCE_MODE: it adds the published ports of the mode, then
# compose.override.yml with your local compose changes (install.sh creates
# it; upgrade.sh never touches it).
#   tls:   COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:compose.tls.yml:compose.override.yml
#   proxy: COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:compose.proxy.yml:compose.override.yml
# With CADENCE_DB=external, compose.external-db.yml goes after the file of
# the mode, e.g.
#   COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:compose.proxy.yml:compose.external-db.yml:compose.override.yml
# With secrets in files, compose.secrets.yml goes right after the file of the
# mode (before compose.external-db.yml), e.g.
#   COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:compose.tls.yml:compose.secrets.yml:compose.override.yml
COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:compose.tls.yml:compose.override.yml

# tls mode: the public host name and the address Let's Encrypt writes to
# when renewal fails.
SDLC_DOMAIN=cadence.example.com
ACME_EMAIL=admin@example.com

# proxy mode: where Caddy listens on the host. Loopback suits a proxy on the
# same machine; for a proxy elsewhere use e.g. 0.0.0.0:8080 and a firewall.
CADENCE_HTTP_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080

# --- database -----------------------------------------------------------------
# bundled   the postgres container of this stack, data in the postgres volume.
# external  your own PostgreSQL 15-18 at SDLC_DATABASE_URL; no postgres
#           container. Written by install.sh --external-db; COMPOSE_FILE then
#           lists compose.external-db.yml after the file of the mode
#           (docs/admin.md, "External PostgreSQL").
CADENCE_DB=bundled
# external: postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE?sslmode=verify-full&sslrootcert=/secrets/db-ca.pem
# (the CA lives in ./secrets, mounted as /secrets). Empty in the bundled mode.
SDLC_DATABASE_URL=
# Or the URL in a file of ./secrets, with SDLC_DATABASE_URL empty; or the URL
# without a password here and the password in a file (docs/admin.md,
# "Secrets in files"):
# SDLC_DATABASE_URL_FILE=/secrets/db-url
# SDLC_DATABASE_PASSWORD_FILE=/secrets/db-password

# bundled: the role, the password and the database of the postgres container.
POSTGRES_USER=sdlc
# Generated by install.sh (openssl rand -hex 24). Never change it on a live
# volume: the database keeps the password it was created with.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_DB=sdlc

# --- first administrator ------------------------------------------------------
# An empty database has nobody to issue the first token, so it comes from the
# environment. Generated by install.sh: sdlc_ followed by 48 hex digits. Sign
# in with it in the UI and with `clab auth login --with-token`.
SDLC_ADMIN_HANDLE=admin
SDLC_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# --- secrets in files (optional) ----------------------------------------------
# Every secret X above and below also takes X_FILE: the path inside the
# containers of a file whose content is the value (a trailing newline is
# cut). Set one of X and X_FILE, never both: both stop the service on start.
# ./secrets is mounted as /secrets; compose.secrets.yml in COMPOSE_FILE moves
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD and SDLC_ADMIN_TOKEN to Docker secrets. Owners, modes and
# the move from .env: docs/admin.md, "Secrets in files". For example:
# SDLC_ADMIN_TOKEN_FILE=/secrets/admin_token
# SDLC_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET_FILE=/secrets/github-webhook-secret
# SDLC_GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE=/secrets/github-client-secret
# SDLC_GITHUB_TOKEN_FILE=/secrets/github-token
# SDLC_EMBEDDINGS_API_KEY_FILE=/secrets/embeddings-api-key
# SDLC_VOYAGE_API_KEY_FILE=/secrets/voyage-api-key
# SDLC_BLOB_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID_FILE=/secrets/blob-s3-key-id
# SDLC_BLOB_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_FILE=/secrets/blob-s3-secret-key
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS_FILE=/secrets/otlp-headers

# --- profile --------------------------------------------------------------------
# single: a dedicated instance of one company - no personal teams, no plans or
# quotas. Keep it.
SDLC_TENANCY=single
# teams: projects are created inside teams, by the administrator and by team
# leads allowed to do so. open would let anyone who signs in create one.
SDLC_PROJECT_CREATION=teams
# token: people and agents authenticate with tokens and sessions. Never
# switch to header outside local debugging - it trusts any caller.
SDLC_AUTH_MODE=token
# Optional first team, created on start (key and display name). Without it
# the administrator creates teams with `clab team create`.
SDLC_BOOTSTRAP_TEAM=
SDLC_BOOTSTRAP_TEAM_NAME=
# Seeds for an empty database. Keep empty: projects, roles and cycles are
# created by your teams. default_workflow adds a demo cycle as a sample.
SDLC_SEED=

# --- sign-in with GitHub (optional) -------------------------------------------
# OAuth credentials of your GitHub App (docs/admin.md, "GitHub App").
# Callback URLs: https://<host>/login/github and
# https://<host>/settings/github/callback. Empty - no GitHub button.
SDLC_GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
SDLC_GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# The app slug from github.com/apps/<slug>: enables "Connect GitHub".
SDLC_GITHUB_APP_SLUG=

# --- repository access (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# GitHub App ID and its private key. Put the key into ./secrets/github-app.pem;
# the directory is mounted as /secrets, so the value below stays as is.
SDLC_GITHUB_APP_ID=
SDLC_GITHUB_APP_KEY_FILE=
# SDLC_GITHUB_APP_KEY_FILE=/secrets/github-app.pem
# Fallback without an app: one read-only token for all repositories.
SDLC_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Webhook signature secret. Generated by install.sh; enter the same value in
# the app settings, webhook URL https://<host>/webhooks/github.
SDLC_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# GitHub Enterprise Cloud with data residency or a proxy: other endpoints.
# SDLC_GITHUB_URL=https://github.com
# SDLC_GITHUB_API_URL=https://api.github.com

# --- sign-in with your identity provider (optional) ---------------------------
# OpenID Connect issuer URL and the client ID of a public client (PKCE, no
# secret). Redirect URI: https://<host>/login. Team membership is synced from
# the groups claim.
SDLC_OIDC_ISSUER=
SDLC_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# SDLC_OIDC_GROUPS_CLAIM=groups

# --- embeddings (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# none: full-text search only, no external calls. Others: voyage, openai
# (any OpenAI-compatible server: OpenAI, Ollama, TEI, vLLM). The model must
# return 1024-dimensional vectors. See docs/admin.md, "Embeddings".
SDLC_EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER=none
# Required for openai, there is no default; voyage defaults to voyage-code-3.
SDLC_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL=
# Base URL of the API, e.g. http://ollama:11434/v1. Empty: the provider's own.
SDLC_EMBEDDINGS_URL=
SDLC_EMBEDDINGS_API_KEY=
# false for servers that reject the `dimensions` field.
SDLC_EMBEDDINGS_SEND_DIMENSIONS=true
# Voyage key; with it and an empty provider, voyage is chosen.
SDLC_VOYAGE_API_KEY=

# --- artifact content (optional) ----------------------------------------------
# Empty bucket: large artifact content lives in the `blobs` volume and
# backup.sh archives it. With a bucket it lives in S3 and the bucket is
# yours to back up.
SDLC_BLOB_S3_BUCKET=
SDLC_BLOB_S3_ENDPOINT=
SDLC_BLOB_S3_REGION=
SDLC_BLOB_S3_PREFIX=
SDLC_BLOB_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
SDLC_BLOB_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- backups (optional) -------------------------------------------------------
# backup.sh (and clab server backup) writes backups/ and keeps them KEEP_DAYS
# days on this machine:
# BACKUP_DIR=backups
# KEEP_DAYS=14
# Off-machine copy: with a bucket, every backup also goes to S3 (AWS, MinIO,
# Cloudflare R2, Yandex Object Storage and other S3-compatible storage) and the
# bucket keeps the newest BACKUP_S3_KEEP backups. Empty bucket: no copy.
# Use a bucket (or a prefix) and keys of their own, allowed to put, get, list
# and delete objects there only (docs/admin.md, "Off-machine copy").
BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=
# Empty: the AWS endpoint of the region, https://s3.<region>.amazonaws.com.
BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=
# Empty: us-east-1.
BACKUP_S3_REGION=
# A "directory" in the bucket, e.g. cadence/ (empty: the root of the bucket).
BACKUP_S3_PREFIX=
BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Or the keys in files of ./secrets, readable by the user that runs
# backup.sh (docs/admin.md, "Secrets in files"):
# BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID_FILE=/secrets/backup-s3-key-id
# BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_FILE=/secrets/backup-s3-secret-key
# true (empty): endpoint/bucket/key - MinIO and most S3-compatible storage;
# false: bucket.endpoint/key.
BACKUP_S3_PATH_STYLE=
# How many backups the bucket keeps (empty: 14); backups before an upgrade
# count too.
BACKUP_S3_KEEP=

# --- monitoring (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# Prometheus metrics of the API and the worker (since v0.10.0) listen on this
# address inside the compose network: http://api:9090/metrics and
# http://worker:9090/metrics. Nothing is published to the host and Caddy
# does not serve /metrics; docs/admin.md, "Monitoring", shows how to let
# Prometheus in. Unset: :9090. Empty: no metrics listener.
# SDLC_METRICS_ADDR=:9090
#
# Traces of the API requests (since v0.12.0), sent over OTLP/HTTP to your
# OpenTelemetry collector or APM. Off while no endpoint is set; gRPC is not
# supported. The worker is not traced. Spans carry the method, the route
# template and the status code, never paths, queries, headers or bodies;
# docs/admin.md, "Monitoring", "Tracing".
# The collector base URL; the API posts to <endpoint>/v1/traces.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4318
# Headers for the collector, e.g. an APM key: key1=value1,key2=value2, a
# value %-encoded (Bearer%20xyz). A secret: or OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS_FILE
# (since v0.13.0). A malformed pair stops the API on start.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=
# otlp turns traces on without an endpoint (then https://localhost:4318),
# none turns them off with one.
# OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=
# service.name of the spans (empty: cadence-api); service.version is always
# the version of the installation.
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=
# More resource attributes: deployment.environment=prod,team=platform.
# OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES=
# Sampling (empty: parentbased_always_on, every request): e.g.
# parentbased_traceidratio with OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=0.1 for 10%.
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=
# OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=

# --- audit log ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Every MCP tool call and every change through the API is written to the
# audit log (docs/admin.md, "Audit log"). The worker deletes entries older
# than this many days, hourly. 0 keeps the log forever; it then grows the
# database and every backup without a bound.
SDLC_AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS=180

# --- tuning (optional) --------------------------------------------------------
# Database connections of each process: the API and the worker hold a pool
# each, so the stack opens up to 2 x SDLC_DB_MAX_CONNS (and as many again per
# extra API replica). Keep the sum below max_connections of an external server.
# SDLC_DB_MAX_CONNS=10
# How long a process waits for the database on start.
# SDLC_DB_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=30s
# SDLC_LOG_LEVEL=info
# SDLC_SESSION_TTL=12h
# SDLC_LEASE_TTL=30m
# SDLC_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL=5m
# SDLC_INDEX_INTERVAL=5m

# --- images (optional) --------------------------------------------------------
# A registry mirror that holds sdlc-pipeline-backend and sdlc-pipeline-frontend.
# The version is never set here: it comes from the VERSION file.
# CADENCE_REGISTRY=ghcr.io/cadence-lab-tech
# What the scripts and clab server do with the signatures of a release
# before they install or upgrade (docs/admin.md, "Verifying a release"):
# auto verifies with cosign 3.x when it is installed and warns once when it
# is not; require also refuses without cosign, an unsigned version, an image
# without a digest and an unreachable ghcr.io; off does not verify (a closed
# network). A signature that does not verify stops both auto and require.
# Set here, it wins over the environment.
# CADENCE_VERIFY=auto
